# Files Wrangler must not upload as public assets.
#
# Astro copies public/ into the build output, so this lands in dist/client — which is the assets
# directory wrangler.jsonc points at, and where .assetsignore has to be to take effect.
#
# wrangler.json is emitted into the output by @cloudflare/vite-plugin. It is an internal build
# artifact containing absolute paths from the build machine, and without this line it would be
# publicly fetchable at /wrangler.json.
wrangler.json

# Belt and braces. This deployment has no `main`, and a build with zero on-demand routes emits
# neither of these today — but if a route ever opts into `prerender = false`, the adapter will
# start emitting a Worker entry, and shipping it as a static asset would expose server code.
_worker.js
_routes.json
